-- title:
--   Fricke twist of δ lands in 𝔪-torsion differentials
-- statement:
--   Fix $M\ge 1$ and assume the operators `heckeOperatorBar M` on $J_0(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ commute pairwise, so that `HeckeAlg` $=\mathbb Z[X_\ell:\ell\text{ prime}]$ acts on `JZero M`. Let $p$ be a prime with $p\nmid M$ and $\mathfrak m\subset$ `HeckeAlg` a maximal ideal containing $p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa$ has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed; assume $F=\kappa(\,\tilde\jmath,\tilde\jmath_M)$, the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`, is a curve over $\kappa$ (principal divisors exist, finite residue extensions, $\Omega_{F/\kappa}$ free of rank one), is essentially of finite type, has characteristic $p$, has $v.dCoord$ generating $\Omega_{F/\kappa}$ at every place $v$, and equals `modularFunctionFieldFullC` $\kappa$ $M$ (the field generated by all $q$-expansions $\tilde\jmath(q^d)$, $d\mid M$), this identification being $hE$. Let $\delta$ be an additive map from the $p$-torsion of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/\kappa)$ to $\Omega_{F/\kappa}$ obeying Serre's recipe: $\delta y=g^{-1}\,dg$ whenever $y$ is the class of a degree-zero divisor $E$ and $g\ne 0$ satisfies $p\,E(v)=\mathrm{ord}_v(g)$ at every place $v$. Let `Fam` be a commuting family of $\kappa$-linear endomorphisms of $\kappa((q))$ indexed by the primes with $\mathrm{Fam}.T_\ell=U_\ell+\ell\,V_\ell$ for $\ell\nmid M$ and $\mathrm{Fam}.T_\ell=U_\ell$ for $\ell\mid M$, let $e:$ `HeckeAlg`$/\mathfrak m\to\kappa$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $w$ be a $\kappa$-algebra automorphism of $F$ interchanging $\tilde\jmath$ and $\tilde\jmath_M$. Finally let $x\in$ `JZero M` be annihilated by $\mathfrak m$, and let $y$ be a $p$-torsion class of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/\kappa)$ whose image under the isomorphism induced by $hE$ is the reduction $\mathrm{red}_A(x)$. Then the pullback of $\delta y$ along $w$ lies in `mTorsionDiffOf`: it is a regular differential (at each place of the form $f\cdot v.dCoord$ with $f$ in the valuation ring) whose image under `qExpansionDiffAlong` is killed by $\mathrm{Fam}$ evaluated at every polynomial over $\mathbb F_p$ vanishing at the system $\ell\mapsto e(X_\ell\bmod\mathfrak m)$.
--
--   This is the transfer step, in the style of Mazur's analysis of the Eisenstein ideal and of Serre's description of $p$-torsion in the Jacobian in characteristic $p$, which converts an $\mathfrak m$-torsion point of $J_0(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ into a regular differential on the special fibre whose $q$-expansion is an eigenform-like vector for the system of Hecke eigenvalues $e(X_\ell \bmod \mathfrak m)$; the Fricke twist by $w$ compensates for the fact that Serre's $\delta$ transports a Hecke correspondence to its transpose. It feeds the bound on the rank of the $\mathfrak m$-torsion of $J_0(M)$ modulo the kernel of reduction.
